---
layout: null
permalink: /sitemap.xml
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Hand-written sitemap, replacing jekyll-sitemap.

  The plugin submitted 2,892 URLs, of which 220 were listing pages with no
  content of their own: 219 paginated index pages (/page2/ ... /page220/) and
  /search/. Google asks that those be kept out of a sitemap, and submitting
  them spends crawl attention that these ~2,400 posts need.

  The plugin has no exclusion hook for the paginated pages, because
  jekyll-paginate clones index.html's front matter onto each one -- a
  `sitemap: false` there would have dropped the homepage too. So the rule here
  is a whitelist instead of a blacklist: a page is listed only if it declares a
  `title`. index.html deliberately has none (its hero text lives in `hero`),
  which excludes every paginated clone; 404.html, offline.html, feed.xml,
  search-data.json and this file have none either. The homepage is added by
  hand below.

  site.sitemap_extra carries the static HTML that lives outside Jekyll's page
  collection -- the deltabrief-site/ and wraith-site/ product pages, which have
  no front matter and so never appear in site.pages. jekyll-sitemap did list
  them, and delisting them would quietly change another product's indexing, so
  they are named explicitly in _config.yml.

  uri_escape then xml_escape reproduces the plugin's encoding: spaces become
  %20, and the ampersands that 213 of these URLs contain become &amp; as XML
  requires.

  NOTE: no Liquid tags inside HTML comments in this repo -- Liquid runs before
  HTML parsing, so braces there still execute. This is a Liquid comment block,
  which is safe.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}/</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ site.posts.first.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
  </url>
{%- for post in site.posts %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ post.url | uri_escape | prepend: site.url | xml_escape }}</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ post.last_modified_at | default: post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
  </url>
{%- endfor %}
{%- for p in site.pages %}
{%- if p.title and p.sitemap != false and p.url != "/" %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ p.url | uri_escape | prepend: site.url | xml_escape }}</loc>
{%- if p.last_modified_at %}
    <lastmod>{{ p.last_modified_at | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
  </url>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for extra in site.sitemap_extra %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ extra | uri_escape | prepend: site.url | xml_escape }}</loc>
  </url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
